 "sector": "Government bond",
 "profiles": [
  {
   "from": "1975-01",
   "tagline": "Lend the US government money and get 100 back on 1 January 1995.",
   "about": "A promise by the US Treasury to pay 100 dollars on 1 January 1995. It pays nothing before that, so it costs less than 100 today and the difference is your interest. If interest rates rise in the meantime the price falls, and if they fall it rises; the further away 1995 is, the stronger the effect. Held until 1995, it pays exactly what was promised."
  }
